INSERT INTO `press` VALUES (30,'Design Trends for 2019 – Expert Insight','','','design-trends-for-2019-expert-insight','Design Trends for 2019 – Expert Insight','/public/upload/press/30/cd8d9d5c7a2eeae889df2d441164d64f','We asked talented local designers and architects: “In your opinion, what are the upcoming interior design trends for 2019, and which is your favorite?”','<p><strong>Materials and textures&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;We are finding that exposed wood, natural materials, (such as hardwood floors, tile and stone) and crisp, simple details are the most requested items we are seeing. We also see a trend towards smaller-space living&hellip; away from the &lsquo;formal dining room&rsquo; to a concept of spaces having multiple uses. This reduces square footage, wasted space, costs for heating, cleaning, and furnishing, while still allowing all the conveniences and opportunities of modern living.&rdquo; &ndash; Craig Martin (AIA, NCARB, LEED AP) and Kurt Shepard &ndash; SPIRE Architecture</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;2018 was a good year for mosaic tiling, and 2019 will continue this trend in full force. Mosaic tiles are so trendy right now that they may soon replace regular bathroom tiles in overall popularity. They will certainly continue to adorn bathroom walls and showers everywhere, but it doesn&rsquo;t end there. Mosaic tiles will power past the bathroom and extend to virtually every other room imaginable in 2019. It&rsquo;s already happening.&rdquo; &ndash; Pavel Abaev &ndash; Basement Masters www.basementremodeling.com</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Cut agate and natural stone accents are still popular in home d&eacute;cor. From gorgeous deep purple cut agate clocks to items such as; coasters, tabletops and chandeliers. Use stone sparingly. Choose one piece as an accent.</p>\r\n<p>Lacquer and acrylic are being used in home furnishings, from acrylic table legs to trays. Heavily lacquered dressers, and accent tables are plentiful. You&rsquo;ll also see a mix of trends, such as a decorative lacquer box with a cut agate stone on top for extra detail.</p>\r\n<p>My favorite trend is acrylic. I love using acrylic furnishings and accents such as trays in small spaces to keep rooms looking open, fresh and modern, plus it&rsquo;s durable!&rdquo;&rdquo; &ndash; Sharon E. O&rsquo;Brien, IDS&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;My personal favorite deals with fabrics &amp; patterns. I love infusing a minimum of at least nine different fabrics and textiles into each room I design for my clients. A vibrant mix of these softer elements that &lsquo;play well&rsquo; with each other is the launching point. I then add in the supporting players with pillow welting, pillow backing, drapery banding and more to complete the look.</p>\r\n<p>I can introduce a variety of fabric textures such as cotton, linen, leather, wool, silk, microfibers, and so on in an appealing combination to achieve a look that is not only visually interactive but also tangibly pleasing to each client.</p>\r\n<p>This blending of fabrics and patterns adds a beautiful dimension to each room design, enhancing the ambiance of exciting colors, a timeless room design, natural woods, and bold metallics.&rdquo; &ndash; Karen Haggard, Owner, Grey Heron Interiors</p>\r\n<p><strong>Design Direction and Themes&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;This year, mixing old and new design concepts is going to be way in style. This is already happening in the Washington-Bethesda area, which is deeply rooted in American history and incorporates many traditional styles into its interior designs. Retro trends and vintage looks will resurface and merge with contemporary furnishings and building materials in the ultimate cultural fusion.&rdquo; &ndash; Pavel Abaev &ndash; Basement Masters</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;I personally love the industrial look and all the interesting accessories that can go with this style. Mixing and matching simple looks is a great thing to do as well. Eclectic has always worked when done tastefully. Interior Design has become very relaxed in its rules, making for very comfortable living spaces.&rdquo; &ndash; Brigitte Steinhorn, Owner, Centsable Designs. Nominated &ldquo;Top Go-Getter 2019&rdquo; by Bethesda Magazine</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;My favorite new design trend is the free-spirited layering of patterns, styles and cultures. Combining years of travel with our design expertise brings this decorating approach right to our doorstep! We&rsquo;re all for featuring our client&rsquo;s personal styles then folding and layering it into an exciting new d&eacute;cor.&rdquo; &ndash; Deb Sagerholm &ndash; Marco Polo&rsquo;s Expeditions in Interior Design</p>\r\n<p><strong>Use of Space&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Although we continue to design large estates, we have also seen an interest in downsizing from large homes to luxury condo units or new smaller homes. In concert with that trend has been a focus on multiple use and efficient use of space. Rooms equipped with a hidden Murphy bed transform an office or studio into a guest room, with no added space. Rooms such as dining rooms double as libraries.</p>\r\n<p>A common thread is that all of our designs attempt to ameliorate the problems unique to each project and to celebrate the potential of each commission. Universal principles of design and response to context remain important influences on the final design.&rdquo; &ndash; Greg Wiedemann, AIA, Principal &ndash; Wiedemann Architects</p>\r\n<p><strong>Furniture, Furnishings and Features&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Keep furniture lines and accessories simple. Mixing more modern and transitional looks with simplicity and the mid-century/industrial trend is also fun to do.&rdquo; &ndash; Brigitte Steinhorn &ndash; Centsable Designs</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Mid-century modern furnishings, mixed with faux fur throws and stone topped tables is still going strong as an appealing look for the millennial generation.&rdquo; &ndash; Sharon E. O&rsquo;Brien, IDS, Inspired Interiors</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;My favorite design trend is to remove the mantle. Until now, the evolution of the fireplace was stunted. Even as wood logs were replaced with clean burning gas inserts, they were just a fossilized version of their ancestors.</p>\r\n<p>Designers began to break away from the more traditional fireplace surrounds and even log sets were replaced by streamlined gas jets sprouting from a puddle of glass or stone. But a reclaimed wood beam or sleek steel fin often remained, hearkening back to the traditional.</p>\r\n<p>Finally, we have released ourselves from the required projection above the beautiful bare flame. No longer is the fire relegated to the lower third of the wall. With no mantle weighing it down, it joins us at eye level or table height, and I delight in its elevated position.&rdquo; &ndash; Margaret Gaughan Upton, AIA &ndash; Principal &ndash; Upton Architecture, LLC</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/4/bb161fe770134cc298c562f7e10ab73d_1000x539.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"900\" height=\"485\" /></p>\r\n<pre>Photo credit: Ken Wyner Photography</pre>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Some popular trends we&rsquo;ve seen are tile floors that resemble wood in a variety of different colors, wood countertops coming back into vogue and square recessed lights in lieu of large round ones. My favorite trend has to be the tiles that look like wood floors allowing those areas that contain it to work well with wood floors within the house&rdquo;. &ndash; Jonathan Rivera Architecture</p>\r\n<p><strong>Colour and patterns&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;The colors for 2019 are still neutrals, your grays, beiges, white shades, soft green hues, and a pop of color. The jewel tones are moving their way back in slowly as style trends. The blue tones are bigger than ever this year. I like the muted color tones with pops of bright colors and bright art work for walls. There are no limits in design!.&rdquo; &ndash; Brigitte Steinhorn &ndash; Centsable Designs</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;In my opinion all shades of blues and greens will continue to be seen in the 2019 color palette. Also, my darling neutral &ndash; Grey &mdash; is still very popular.&rdquo; &ndash; Deb Sagerholm &ndash; Marco Polo&rsquo;s Expeditions in Interior Design</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;This last interior design trend is my personal favorite. The standard and long-favored traditional white is being replaced by more dramatic colors, both bright and dark. Striking greens and purples are becoming the norm instead of being reserved for the occasional accent wall. We have been doing this for some time and it always creates a well-received response.&rdquo; &ndash; Pavel Abaev &ndash; Basement Masters</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;For 2019 expect to see a lot of gold leaf accents in home d&eacute;cor. From cabinet hardware to mirrors, trays, tables, sculpture, and art objects. Gold has been showing up everywhere and is continuing its resurgence! With the Pantone color of the year being &lsquo;Greenery 15-0343&rsquo;, which is a bright happy revitalizing shade of green, you&rsquo;ll see this color popping up in home d&eacute;cor and painted on walls. Expect to see it paired with black and white accents.</p>\r\n<p>Another trend that is hot and appearing everywhere is butterflies. From gorgeous hand screened wallpaper, lamps, fabrics, and tableware. Butterflies are on the move in 2019!&rdquo; &ndash; Sharon E. O&rsquo;Brien, IDS, Inspired Interiors</p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;You&rsquo;ll see the jewel tone colors of Green, Blue, Purple, deep Terracotta everywhere. Designers are rethinking Beige for a go to neutral as a refreshing update to Gray. Lastly you can&rsquo;t go wrong with a White upholstered or slip covered stain resistant sofa. Bring in the color using plaid throws, patterned pillows, area rug, rustic accents or a tartan chair to mix things up&rdquo; &ndash; Vickie Williams &ndash; House to Home</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/5/94d679d3f193dff1abbe87159101c2c3_936x678.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"936\" height=\"678\" /></p>\r\n<pre>Image Credit: Vickie Williams &ndash; House to Home</pre>\r\n<p><strong>Technology&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Technology continues to evolve and clients are able to monitor and have control of the systems of their homes such as lighting, audio, and video from their smart phones. Remote access of mechanical, electrical, and security systems allows our clients of second homes to monitor their homes from a distance. Remote sensors can make homes more responsive to changes over time.&rdquo; &ndash; Greg Wiedemann, AIA, Principal &ndash; Wiedemann Architects</p>\r\n<p><strong>In the Kitchen&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Design Trends that are sure to last a good 5 years. White and wood kitchens&hellip;..I love the clean, open refreshing feel of a white kitchen particularly (white cabinets with wood floors or wood counter tops.) The surfaces are easier to clean since you can actually see the grime while wood accents will add warmth contrasting the cool whites, thus making this , my top choice of design trends. Consumers are also turning to Quartz and Soapstone for the same reason.&rdquo; &ndash; Vickie Williams &ndash; House to Home</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/6/9af6a97ae9836b99f4743e0a6c603d76_740x493.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"740\" height=\"493\" /></p>\r\n<pre>Image Credit: Vickie Williams &ndash; House to Home</pre>\r\n<p><strong>In the Bathroom&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;A particular trend that shows no sign of slowing up is adding luxury to bathrooms. Treats like heated floors, skylights, personalized storage, make-up desks, step-in steam showers, Japanese soaking tubs and even a chandelier have found their way into this room. We know that there&rsquo;s always a bit of space for a little self-indulgence no matter what the bathroom size!&rdquo; &ndash; Deb Sagerholm &ndash; Marco Polo&rsquo;s Expeditions in Interior Design</p>\r\n<p><strong>In the Bedroom&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;You&rsquo;ll see Upholstered Head boards replacing the solid wood bed frames thus adding an element of elegance, softness and color to the otherwise all wood matching furnishings. Marrying soft and hard furniture pieces together makes for a cozier relaxing room. I&rsquo;m also noticing modern and nomadic styles being used to create a fun colorful inviting living space. A mix of contemporary, mid century modern pieces with bold art statements brings a room to life.&rdquo; &ndash; Vickie Williams &ndash; House to Home</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"../../../../public/upload/custom/7/171a44ab959ca16d50eab8e50c0da9a7_640x881.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"568\" height=\"786\" /></p>\r\n<pre>Image Credit: Vickie Williams &ndash; House to Home</pre>\r\n<p><strong>Out in the Great Outdoors&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;Creating indoor/outdoor spaces with materials that flow across exterior wall planes is one of our favorite trends.&rdquo; &ndash; Craig Martin and Kurt Shepard &ndash; SPIRE Architecture</p>\r\n<p><strong>The Environment&hellip;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&ldquo;There continues to be an interest in the use of green products, such as locally sourced materials and sustainable products such as bamboo flooring. Authenticity and the use of natural materials remain important to our clients.&rdquo; &ndash; Greg Wiedemann, AIA, Principal &ndash; Wiedemann Architects</p>\r\n<p><strong>Our Point of View&hellip;</strong> No two years are even remotely the same in the world of interior design &ndash; and we&rsquo;re excited and challenged in equal measure by this rapidly changing world. Of course, as a green-focused company, we are watching with interest as interior design becomes ever more environmentally focused &ndash; with beautiful homes, that take into account our beautiful planet. From the exposed wood and natural materials that will be seen in our flooring, tile and stone, to the colours that will be introduced in the way of greys, greens and blues, it appears that nature is going to play a big role in our homes this year. The Scandinavian, stripped back to basics theme is in full swing, and we feel that this industrial design direction, in all its simplicity, will work hand in glove with the &lsquo;au natural&rsquo; theme, and it can only make the role of materials and colours all the more important. It will be interesting to see how these design directions play along with the focus on gold and luxurious fittings and fixtures &ndash; it may be that gold is used only in limited amounts, such as in a single statement piece per room, or restricted to the detailing on home accessories. We also think that technology will play an increasingly important role within interior design in 2019. Not only are we starting to see just what Smart tech is capable of when it comes to making our lives easier, we&rsquo;re also hopeful as to what it can bring in terms of home energy efficiency.</p>\r\n<p>Safe to say that 2019 will be an enthralling year for those of us who are avid interior design fans, and we&rsquo;d like to say thanks to all of our design and interior experts in sharing their thoughts with us. If you fancy yourself as an armchair interior expert (and have predictions of your own), share them with us in the comments below.</p>','The Greener Living Blog','https://www.ambientbp.com/blog/design-trends-for-2017-expert-insight',0,'2019-01-15 09:19:34'),(31,'Basement Masters to Expand Operations to Baltimore Area and Beyond','','','basement-masters to Expand Operations to Baltimore Area and Beyond','Basement Masters to Expand Operations to Baltimore Area and Beyond','/public/upload/press/31/e4e7e719a4d4bcaa9d5acea63b22ec63','Basement Masters, a commercial and residential basement remodeling company, announced today the expansion of its services into Greater Baltimore, with plans to incorporate the state of New York next.','<p><strong>Basement Masters, a commercial and residential basement remodeling company, announced today the expansion of its services into Greater Baltimore, with plans to incorporate the state of New York next.</strong></p>\n<p>ROCKVILLE, MD, February 22, 2017 /Building and Construction PR News/ -- This decision comes after a sharp increase of quotes in both regions prompted Basement Masters to seek two new partners. Now they will be able to remodel basements in Baltimore, Carrol, Howard, Harford and Anne Arundel counties.</p>\n<p>\"We did a great job finding two new partners to meet our high standards and growing demand,\" says Pavel Abaev, Founder and CEO at Basement Masters. \"These new partners were checked meticulously - reviews, portfolios, absolutely everything. We are looking forward to working with them so that we can provide Baltimore with the same level of style and professionalism that has made Basement Masters so successful elsewhere in the past.\"</p>\n<p>About Basement Masters</p>\n<p>Basement Masters is the only remodeling company to focus exclusively on basement projects since 2011. Now shifting their attention from residential projects to small-to-medium businesses, Basement Masters looks forward to helping the chosen company in Greater Baltimore expand and residents to embody their desire to finish an unfinished or remodel their basement while simultaneously expanding themselves. Visit the company website at www.basementremodeling.com for helpful advice. Phone: 301-798-4444</p>','Construction PR News','',1,'2017-02-22 10:24:03'),(32,'Houzz Awards Basement Masters ','','','houzz-awards-basement-masters-best-of-custome-service-achievement-for-2016','Houzz Awards Basement Masters ','/public/upload/press/32/d5642e1a3b7bf57974529a9bce3619a4','This year, Basement Masters rises above more than one million other home construction, remodeling, and design industry professionals to claim the \"Best of Customer Service\" award for 2016, and more than 35 million monthly Houzz subscribers agree.','<p><strong>Over 35 Million Houzz Users Nominate the Best Home Building, Remodeling and Design Professionals in North America and Beyond</strong></p>\n<p>ROCKVILLE, MD, April 23, /ABC6 NEWS -- According to Houzz, the largest online community for home remodeling and design, one family-owned company servicing the Maryland and Virginia area stands out from the rest. This year, Basement Masters rises above more than one million other home construction, remodeling, and design industry professionals to claim the \"Best of Customer Service\" award for 2016, and more than 35 million monthly Houzz subscribers agree.</p>\n<p>\"Anyone building, remodeling or decorating looks to Houzz for the most talented and service-oriented professionals,\" said Liza Hausman, Vice President of Industry Marketing for Houzz. \"We\'re so pleased to recognize the \'Best of Houzz Service\' award for 2016.\"</p>\n<p>The annual \"Best of Houzz\" awards are divided into in three categories: \"Design\", \"Customer Service\" and \"Photography\". The \"Customer Service\" division, in particular, is based on several factors - most notably, the number of high-quality client reviews from 2015.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>As a sign of their commitment to excellence, an official \"Best of Houzz 2016\" badge will appear on the winners\' profiles. These badges help homeowners identify popular and top-rated home professionals in every metro area on Houzz.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Find out about what the Houzz community has to say about Basement Masters, and why they are the right choice for you.</p>\n<p><strong>About Basement Masters</strong></p>\n<p>In business since 2006, Basement Masters has completed more than 1 thousand projects in 10 years. Ever since deciding to focus exclusively on basements in 2011, the experts at Basement Masters have been hard at work, dutifully servicing the Maryland and Virginia areas. February 2016, is another landmark achievement for them - over 500 successful basement projects.</p>\n<p>\"We are the \'number one\' basement finishing and remodeling company in Maryland and Virginia for one big reason, and one big reason alone,\" says Pavel Abaev, Owner of Basement Masters. \"We pay exceptional attention to details, which allows us to provide the highest quality results at the most competitive prices.\"</p>\n<p>Aside competitive pricing, Pavel Abaev, and the rest of the Basement Masters staff, strongly believes that all of the work should only be done by professionals, which is why they always use experienced sub-contractors who have been performing their trade for many years, and with proven results. The company has been working with the same sub-contractors for years, and their low turnaround rates mean that the team finishing the basements today consists of the same talented personnel as four years ago. In fact, the basement workforce has a combined experience of over 250 years.</p>\n<p>\"We are a 100% \'A-rated\' company,\" adds Pavel Abaev. \"Over a period of almost ten years, we have not received even a single negative review from any client. Only positive recommendations.\"</p>\n<p>Do you need a beautiful basement? Visit Basement Masters website BasementRemodeling.com, find your inspiration and schedule a free consultation.</p>\n<p><strong>About Houzz</strong></p>\n<p>Houzz is the leading online platform for home remodeling and design, providing people with everything they need to improve their homes from start to finish. From decorating a small room to building an entire custom home, Houzz connects millions of homeowners, home design enthusiasts and home improvement professionals from around the world. With the largest residential design database in existence and a vibrant community empowered by the most innovative technology available, Houzz is the easiest way for people to find inspiration, get advice, buy products and hire the professionals they need to help turn their home improvement ideas into reality.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Headquartered in Palo Alto, CA, Houzz also maintains an international presence with offices in London, Berlin, Sydney, Moscow, and Tokyo. Houzz and the Houzz logo are registered trademarks of Houzz Inc., worldwide. Need home advice? What are you waiting for? Find out why Houzz is the leading online platform for all things home-related.&nbsp;</p>','ABC6 NEWS','http://www.abc6.com/story/31798162/houzz-awards-basement-masters-best-of-customer-service-achievement-for-2016',2,'2017-04-23 10:36:48'),(33,'Basement Masters to Achieve New Business Growth in 2017','','','basement-masters-to-achieve-new-business-growth-in-2017','Basement Masters to Achieve New Business Growth in 2017','/public/upload/press/33/1ed3971355f00ba6d2e8babb2a1c5c23','Basement Masters, a basement remodeling company specializing in business and residential projects, recently announced two key partnerships that will help them better serve the state of Maryland and other surrounding areas.','<p>Basement Masters, a basement remodeling company specializing in business and residential projects, recently announced two key partnerships that will help them better serve the state of Maryland and other surrounding areas.</p>\n<p>ROCKVILLE, MD, March 14, 2017 /24-7PressRelease/ -- Basement Masters, a basement remodeling company specializing in business and residential projects, recently announced two key partnerships that will help them better serve the state of Maryland and other surrounding areas.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>\"We very are proud to announce that we will soon be able to service Greater Baltimore,\" said Pavel Abaev, Owner at Basement Masters. \"Specifically, basements in need of remodeling in Baltimore, Carrol, Howard, and Anne Arundel countries will all be within reach.\"&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Though an official announcement is still underway, the two new partners are poised to propel Basement Masters into the state of New York as well.</p>\n<p>\"We conducted a deep background check into each company\'s professional work history and reputation (including portfolios and customer reviews), and we\'re proud to say that they are everything we are looking for and more,\" said Pavel. \"Our dual partners will bring 100% new business growth to Basement Masters.\"</p>\n<p>About Basement Masters</p>\n<p>Basement Masters is the only remodeling company to focus exclusively on basement projects since 2011. Now shifting their attention from residential projects to small-to-medium businesses, Basement Masters looks forward to helping the chosen company in Greater Baltimore expand and residents to embody their desire to finish an unfinished or remodel their basement while simultaneously expanding themselves. Visit the company website at www.basementremodeling.com for helpful advice. Phone: 301-798-4444</p>','24-7 Press Release','http://business.smdailypress.com/smdailypress/news/read/33895577/Basement_Masters_to_Achieve_New_Business_Growth_in_2017',3,'2017-03-14 11:00:12'),(34,'Basement Masters Announces New Website Launch','','','basement-masters-announces-new-website-launch','Basement Masters Announces New Website Launch','/public/upload/press/34/ed2c3fcadae2b2add267d8f10f867d3a','A completely new website offers ideas, inspiration, and crucial information pertaining to the underground world of basement remodeling.','<p>ROCKVILLE, MD, May 07, 2016 /The Olympian/ -- Basement Masters, the premiere basement specialists in Maryland and Virginia, announced today the launch of its newly revamped website. The website, www.basementremodeling.com, presents users with quick and convenient access to essential basement information and other features designed to educate and inspire.</p>\n<p>\"We want to show visitors as much as we can about our process so as to demystify the process of basement remodeling,\" says Oleg Arzamasov, Director of Marketing for Basement Masters. \"On our webpage, you will find that we are a very open company. We are personally responsible for everything we do, and we not afraid to show our faces - along with plenty of pictures of our wonderful work.\"</p>\n<p>Professional photographs can be found in the newly designed \"Portfolio\" section, which also contains beautifully detailed descriptions depicting each project in all its subterranean glory. An interactive map provides the exact geographical location for each successful site for easy tracking. If you need additional suggestions, more inspiration can be found in the \"Basement Ideas\", which focuses on floor space designs, decorative themes, and all aspects of engineering.</p>\n<p>Those completely new to the industry can quickly catch up by visiting the \"Education Center\". Aside from riveting testimonials of clients who have been recently served by Basement Masters (which allows you to learn firsthand what to expect), you will also find helpful questions that you should ask every contractor, tips to avoid common mistakes, and a general overview on how basement remodeling works.</p>\n<p>The website www.basementremodeling.com prominently displays its achievements in the \"Awards\" section, which provides links to popular review sites such as Angie\'s List, Houzz, HomeAdvisor, Facebook, and the Better Business Bureau (BBB).</p>\n<p>\"Visitors can also get a quote online, get a personalized answer to their questions by filling out the \'Contact Us\' form, or they can schedule in-home consultations and showroom visits right through the website,\" Arzamasov says, before thoughtfully adding, \"and they are always welcome to make a call at (301) 798-4444 to speak with us directly.\"</p>\n<p>If you are unable to afford a new basement on your own, the new website proudly offers a wide variety of financing offers - thanks to a burgeoning partnership with GreenSky Credit. You can even get instant approval for up to $55 thousand by applying online!</p>\n<p>Basement Masters began in 2006 as a general contracting company before switching exclusively to basements in 2011. The experts have since remodeled over 500 successful basement projects in Maryland and Virginia during that time. Visit the new company website at www.basementremodeling.com for an inside look at the industry, full of great suggestions and helpful advice.</p>','The Olympian','http://markets.financialcontent.com/mi.theolympian/news/read/32061009/Basement_Masters_Announces_New_Website_Launch',4,'2016-05-07 11:11:15'),(35,'Basement Masters and ValueDry Waterproofing Partnership','','','basement-masters-and-valuedry-waterproofing-partnership','Basement Masters and ValueDry Waterproofing Partnership','/public/upload/press/35/30a05302da1c76c8d629217d5f8c368f','Value Dry Basement Waterproofing and Basement Masters Remodeling partner to deliver protected high end finished basements to homeowners in Washington DC, Suburban Maryland and Northern Virginia.','<p><strong>Value Dry Basement Waterproofing and Basement Masters Remodeling partner to deliver protected high end finished basements to homeowners in Washington DC, Suburban Maryland and Northern Virginia.</strong></p>\n<p>COLUMBIA, Md., March 29, 2016/YAHOO Finance/ -- Value Dry, a full-service basement waterproofing and crawl space encapsulation provider, and Basement Masters, a high-end basement remodeling provider, will refer each others clientele in order to deliver protected custom finished basements.</p>\n<p>\"Value Dry has been looking for over 10 years for a remodeling partner specializing in basements that understands homeowners need to work with a reputable waterproofing company that has reliable on-going service capabilities. Pavel and his team provide homeowners with stunning custom finished basements. Value Dry installs systems that protect finished basements, so this partnership makes perfect sense,\" says James Ketterer, President, at Value Dry Waterproofing.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>\"The basements remodeled by Basement Masters include full tile bathrooms with glass door showers, custom built-ins, wet bars, media rooms, additional bedrooms and even in-law suites across the DC Metropolitan Area. Our customers deserve to work with a reputable basement waterproofing company to protect the investment they make with Basement Masters. Value Dry has the experience, resources and track record to stand behind their warranty and provide ongoing service to our high-end customers,\" says Pavel Abaev, Owner, at Basement Masters.</p>\n<p>Basement Masters and Value Dry will be working hand in hand on basement projects in the DC Metro Area as well as teaming at home improvement trade shows. The partnership will be introduced and showcased April 1st &nbsp;&ndash; 3rd at the Suburban Maryland Home Show, hosted at the Howard County Fairgrounds.</p>\n<p>About Value Dry</p>\n<p>Value Dry is a full-service basement waterproofing and crawl space encapsulation provider in the MD, DC, VA, Kent and Sussex county DE area. Headquartered centrally in Savage, MD, Value Dry can quickly respond to warranty and service issues in its service area. A locally owned and operated company, Value Dry takes pride in its stellar reputation, ongoing customer service, and lifetime transferable warranties. Website www.valuedrywaterproofing.com Phone: 888-709-3309.</p>\n<p>About Basement Masters</p>\n<p>Basement Masters is the industry\'s first remodeling company focused solely on helping our clients achieve the basement they dream about. The dreams we help come true for our clients include custom built-in shelving, wet bars, kitchenettes, media rooms, home gyms, additional basement bedrooms, full and partial basement bathrooms, as well as in-law suites. Website www.basementremodeling.com Phone: 301-945-8155</p>','YAHOO Finance','http://finance.yahoo.com/news/value-dry-basement-waterproofing-basement-143500516.html',5,'2016-03-29 11:17:46');
